                <pb facs="0592" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg512"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lardy to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Manchester, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic">September 15,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President of the Swiss Confederation, after wiring to Mrs. McKinley and
                    calling personally on Mr. Hardy, has sent me the following message: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The Federal Council, deeply moved by the demise of President McKinley,
                            who succumbed to the effects of a heinous attempt, directs that you
                            expressly convey its sympathy to the Government of the Union and to the
                            family of the deceased. The entire Swiss people share these
                            sentiments.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lardy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Chargé d’Affaires of Switzerland</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
